Arguments:
  (none)

Description:
  Displays The Wall, SklaffKOM's connection to IBOL
  (InterBBS Oneliner).

  IBOL is a shared electronic wall where users on different BBS systems
  can post short messages to each other. The most recently received
  messages are shown together with the sender's name, BBS and timestamp.

  After The Wall has been displayed, you are given the option to write
  a line of your own. It is then queued for delivery to the IBOL network
  and may later appear on other connected BBS systems.

Note:
  A line posted to The Wall may contain at most 65 characters.

  The number of lines displayed is configured by the SysOp. The Wall may
  also be disabled completely on systems where IBOL is not in use.

  Messages are not sent directly to a particular user or BBS. Everything
  posted to The Wall is intended to be visible to other participants on
  the IBOL network.

